==== GOLDEN ARTEFACT h60_read/cb702/out/h60_report_discovery.txt | bytes=17872 | sha256=45f7043dede786d0c9400a8060dac8c9e115efe24bd36e6a72026d441156433d | text
#702 h60 - the HOURLY-CLOSE entry read on discovery (2022-03-28..2024-12-31, DECIDES). Registered before any outcome: docs/analysis/cb_hourly_entry_prereg_2026-10-19.md. Measurement only: nothing here switches the deciding entry, a stop outside the stop bar, a cell, a period, the horizon, the n floor, the seed or the draw count.
POPULATION: every row under the pole (spec key, rule (b)); the base's ONE trade = the first break day on which a 60-minute bar closed above the row's line and the next minute's open could fill; cell + period from the FIRST-break row, the day's facts from the CONFIRMING row. Entry h60, stop lod (the day's low through the bar's end), exit c3_p33_t20_cut3 (sell 1/3 at +2R or the session-3 close, breakeven, 20-day trail, stallers cut at the session-3 close), level tl (decides) / com (beside). A group is the MATURE walks only; an open mark is counted, never in a number.
INTERVAL RECIPE (check 6 reproduces it with no runner code): month-block bootstrap of the mean - blocks = calendar months (the FILL month for a cell's trades; the FIRST-break month for a paired delta), 2,000 resamples of as many blocks as there are months, with replacement, each resample's mean = sum of the drawn blocks' R / their trade count; the 2.5 / 97.5 percentiles (numpy.percentile, linear); generator numpy.random.default_rng([702, zlib.crc32(key)]) with key 'h60|<period>|<window>|<cell>|<K>|<entry>|<stop>|<arm>' for a cell and 'h60pair|<period>|<window>|<cell>|entry' / '|entry_first' / '|stop' for the paired deltas (the stream is drawn as integers(0, n_months, size=(2000, n_months))).
DATA CHECKS: freeze passed; STEP 0 equal to the registered table; early-close ok; data-abstain share 0.00%; twin equal in content to trades_discovery_p5.tsv.gz; rows walked 12

========== WINDOW discovery ==========
EXPECTATIONS (fixed before the run; a missed one is reported first and changes NO rule):
  MISSED: C1 n reads 1 (expected 60-90)
  MET: the C0 share stopped on the fill day under h60 reads 0.0% (expected < 25%; ORH5 ~ 35%)
  NO SAME-DAY PAIR: on the 0 same-day C1 pairs the h60 fill sits above ORH5's on 0 (median fill ratio -; the reading chosen for 'sits above': the MEDIAN pair's h60 fill is above ORH5's)
  ORH5 C0 BASELINE from the twin: mean R -1.00, win 0.0%, >= 10R 0.0 per 100 (the registration's numbers: -0.17R, 31%, 0.9 per 100 on discovery)

